Original technical report:
Yuhan Zhang, Zhiyuan Guo, Ziheng Zeng, Wei Wang, Wentao Wu, and Lijie Xu.
Mandol: An Agglomerative Agent Memory System for Long-Term Conversations.
arXiv:2606.29778 (2026), https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.29778.

Competition-specific modifications include independent Textual, Coding and
Multimodal AML APIs; a shared canonical SQLite/publication substrate;
rebuildable Qdrant projections; HTTP inference and checked model contracts;
request replay, physical track isolation and recovery; coding episode evidence;
multimodal image validation, content-addressed media and image restoration.
This is a competition implementation, not the upstream paper artifact.

The substrate's original NOTICE is additionally retained in
packages/substrate/NOTICE. Its historical description does not describe every
later unified-repository change. See docs/ATTRIBUTION.md for the current scope.
Model weights, datasets and separately retrieved AML evaluation sources are not
distributed with this project. External models and dependencies retain their
own licenses/terms.
